jlDensity(x) draws a line plot of a kernel density estimate of x.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vy := map(x +-> coerce(sin(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlDensity(vy)
```

jlDensity!(x) draws a line plot of a kernel density estimate of x on the existing graph object.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vz := map(x +-> coerce(cos(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlDensity!(vz)
```

jlPlot(x,y) draws a plot using elements of x and y.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vy := map(x +-> coerce(sin(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlPlot(vx, vy)
```

jlPlot(x,y,z) draws a plot using elements of x, y and z.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vy := map(x +-> coerce(sin(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
vz := map(x +-> coerce(cos(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlPlot(vx, vy, vz)
```

jlPlot!(x,y) draws a plot using elements of x and y on the existing graph object.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vz := map(x +-> coerce(cos(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlPlot!(vx, vz)
```

jlPlot!(x,y,z) draws a plot using elements of x, y and z on the existing graph object.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vy := map(x +-> coerce(sin(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
vz := map(x +-> coerce(cos(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlPlot!(vx, vz, vy)
```

jlCurves(x,y) draws a Bezier plot curve from (x.1,y.1) to (x.end,y.end) with control points (x.2,y.2),..., (x.end-1,y.end-1) and draws it.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vy := map(x +-> coerce(sin(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlCurves(vx, vy)
```

jlCurves!(x,y) draws a Bezier plot curve from (x.1,y.1) to (x.end,y.end) with control points (x.2,y.2),..., (x.end-1,y.end-1) and draws it on the existing graph object.

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-%pi..%pi, 100);
vz := map(x +-> coerce(cos(x pretend DoubleFloat))@JF64, vx);
jlCurves!(vx, vz)
```

jlBar(x,y) draws a bar plot of y vs x. Example (Standard Normal Distribution):

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 25);
vy := map(x +-> (t := x pretend DoubleFloat; coerce(exp(-t^2/2.0))@JF64), vx);
jlBar(vx, vy)
```

jlBar!(x,y) draws a bar plot of y vs x on the existing graph object. Example (Shifted Gaussian Distribution):

```fricas
vx := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 25);
vz := map(x +-> (t := x pretend DoubleFloat; coerce(0.5*exp(-(t-1.0)^2/2.0))@JF64), vx);
jlBar!(vx, vz)
```

jlWireframe(x,y,mat) draws the wireframe surface of mat.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlWireframe(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlWireframe!(x,y,mat) draws the wireframe surface of mat on the existing graph object.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlWireframe!(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlSurface(x,y,mat) draws the plot surface of mat.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlSurface(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlSurface!(x,y,mat) draws the plot surface of mat on the existing graph object.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlSurface!(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlContour(x,y,mat) draws the contour plot of surface mat.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlContour(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlContour!(x,y,mat) draws the contour plot of surface mat on the existing graph object.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlContour!(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlContourf(x,y,mat) draws the contour plot of surface mat. Fill area between contours.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlContourf(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlContourf!(x,y,mat) draws the contour plot of surface mat on the existing graph object. Fill area between contours.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlContourf!(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlHeatmap(x, y, mat) draws a heatmap of surface mat.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlHeatmap(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlHeatmap!(x, y, mat) adds a heatmap of surface mat on existing graphic.

```fricas
xGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40); yGrid := jlRange(-3.0..3.0, 40);
zMat := qnew(40, 40)$JF64MAT;
jlHeatmap!(xGrid, yGrid, zMat)
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, a..b) draws the 2D parametric curve (fx(t), fy(t)). Example (Astroid Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t)^3;
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t)^3;
jlParametricPlot(f, g, 0.0..6.283)
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, a..b, n) draws the 2D parametric curve using n points. Example (Lissajous 3:4 Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(3.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(4.0*t);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, 0.0..6.283, 200)
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, a..b, title) draws the 2D parametric curve with title. Example (Deltoid Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> 2.0*cos(t) + cos(2.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> 2.0*sin(t) - sin(2.0*t);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, 0.0..6.283, "Deltoid Curve")
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, a..b, n, title) draws the 2D parametric curve with title using n points. Example (Trefoil Knot Projection):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t) + 2.0*sin(2.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t) - 2.0*cos(2.0*t);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, 0.0..6.283, 200, "Trefoil Projection (200 pts)")
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, fz, a..b) draws the 3D space curve (fx(t), fy(t), fz(t)). Example (Circular Helix):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t / 5.0;
jlParametricPlot(f, g, h, 0.0..18.85)
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, fz, a..b, n) draws the 3D space curve using n points. Example (Trefoil Knot):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t) + 2.0*sin(2.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t) - 2.0*cos(2.0*t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> -sin(3.0*t);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, h, 0.0..6.283, 200)
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, fz, a..b, title) draws the 3D space curve with title. Example (Viviani's Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> 1.0 + cos(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> 2.0*sin(t/2.0);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, h, -6.283..6.283, "Viviani's Curve")
```

jlParametricPlot(fx, fy, fz, a..b, n, title) draws the 3D space curve with title using n points. Example (Toroidal Spiral Knot):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> (2.0 + cos(10.0*t))*cos(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> (2.0 + cos(10.0*t))*sin(t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(10.0*t);
jlParametricPlot(f, g, h, 0.0..6.283, 300, "Toroidal Spiral Knot (300 pts)")
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, a..b) adds the 2D parametric curve on existing plot. Example (Unit Circle):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, 0.0..6.283)
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, a..b, n) adds the 2D parametric curve using n points. Example (Lemniscate of Gerono):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t)*cos(t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, 0.0..6.283, 150)
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, a..b, title) adds the 2D parametric curve with title. Example (Logarithmic Spiral):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> exp(t/10.0)*cos(t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> exp(t/10.0)*sin(t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, 0.0..18.85, "Logarithmic Spiral")
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, a..b, n, title) adds the 2D parametric curve with title using n points. Example (Lissajous 5:6 Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(5.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(6.0*t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, 0.0..6.283, 300, "Lissajous 5:6 (300 pts)")
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, fz, a..b) adds the 3D space curve on existing plot. Example (Conical Helix):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t*cos(2.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t*sin(2.0*t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t;
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, h, 0.0..12.57)
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, fz, a..b, n) adds the 3D space curve using n points. Example (Twisted Cubic Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t;
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t^2;
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> t^3;
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, h, -1.5..1.5, 100)
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, fz, a..b, title) adds the 3D space curve with title. Example (Baseball Seam Curve):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(t) + 0.4*sin(3.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(t) - 0.4*cos(3.0*t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> 0.8*sin(2.0*t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, h, 0.0..6.283, "Baseball Seam Curve")
```

jlParametricPlot!(fx, fy, fz, a..b, n, title) adds the 3D space curve with title using n points. Example (3D Lissajous Knot):

```fricas
f := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(2.0*t);
g := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> sin(3.0*t);
h := (t : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> cos(5.0*t);
jlParametricPlot!(f, g, h, 0.0..6.283, 250, "3D Lissajous Knot (250 pts)")
```

jlVectorField(u, v, a..b, c..d) draws the 2D vector field (u(x, y), v(x, y)). Example (Rotational Vortex / Harmonic Oscillator):

```fricas
f := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> -v;
g := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> u;
jlVectorField(f, g, -2.0..2.0, -2.0..2.0)
```

jlVectorField(u, v, a..b, c..d, n) draws the 2D vector field using an n by n grid. Example (Hyperbolic Saddle Field):

```fricas
f := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> u;
g := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> -v;
jlVectorField(f, g, -2.0..2.0, -2.0..2.0, 20)
```

jlVectorField(u, v, a..b, c..d, title) draws the 2D vector field with title. Example (Van der Pol Oscillator Field):

```fricas
f := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> v;
g := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> (1.0 - u^2)*v - u;
jlVectorField(f, g, -3.0..3.0, -3.0..3.0, "Van der Pol Oscillator")
```

jlVectorField(u, v, a..b, c..d, n, title) draws the 2D vector field with title using an n by n grid. Example (Lotka-Volterra Predator-Prey Field):

```fricas
f := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> u*(1.5 - v);
g := (u : DoubleFloat, v : DoubleFloat) : DoubleFloat +-> -v*(3.0 - u);
jlVectorField(f, g, 0.0..5.0, 0.0..5.0, 20, "Lotka-Volterra Field (20x20)")
```
